### Appointment API - VS Code REST Client
### Run these top to bottom. Ids from earlier responses feed later requests.

@base = http://localhost:3000

### Health check
GET {{base}}/health

### 1. Create a customer  (phone is normalised to 10 digits)
# @name createCustomer
POST {{base}}/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Gagan V", "phone": "+91 98765-43210", "email": "gagan@example.com" }

### 2. Create a provider
# @name createProvider
POST {{base}}/providers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Dr Rao", "type": "Cardiology" }

### 3. Create a service for that provider
# @name createService
POST {{base}}/services
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Heart consultation",
  "price": 800,
  "durationMinutes": 30,
  "providerId": "{{createProvider.response.body.data._id}}"
}

### 4. Book it. No endTime - it comes from durationMinutes.
# @name createAppointment
POST {{base}}/appointments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "{{createCustomer.response.body.data._id}}",
  "providerId": "{{createProvider.response.body.data._id}}",
  "serviceId":  "{{createService.response.body.data._id}}",
  "startTime":  "2026-12-01T04:30:00.000Z"
}

### 5. THE DEMO MOMENT: a second customer, overlapping start -> 409
# Change the time to 05:00:00.000Z and it succeeds - back-to-back is allowed.
POST {{base}}/appointments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "{{createCustomer.response.body.data._id}}",
  "providerId": "{{createProvider.response.body.data._id}}",
  "serviceId":  "{{createService.response.body.data._id}}",
  "startTime":  "2026-12-01T04:45:00.000Z"
}

### 6. endTime is rejected outright (strict body) -> 400
POST {{base}}/appointments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "{{createCustomer.response.body.data._id}}",
  "providerId": "{{createProvider.response.body.data._id}}",
  "serviceId":  "{{createService.response.body.data._id}}",
  "startTime":  "2026-12-01T06:00:00.000Z",
  "endTime":    "2026-12-01T09:00:00.000Z"
}

### 7. A timestamp with no timezone is rejected -> 400
POST {{base}}/appointments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "{{createCustomer.response.body.data._id}}",
  "providerId": "{{createProvider.response.body.data._id}}",
  "serviceId":  "{{createService.response.body.data._id}}",
  "startTime":  "2026-12-01 10:00"
}

### 8. List with filters (strict: ?providerid= would be a 400)
GET {{base}}/appointments?providerId={{createProvider.response.body.data._id}}&status=booked

### 9. Reschedule (re-runs the clash check, ignoring itself)
PATCH {{base}}/appointments/{{createAppointment.response.body.data._id}}/reschedule
Content-Type: application/json

{ "startTime": "2026-12-01T07:00:00.000Z" }

### 10. Cancel, which frees the slot for a rebooking
PATCH {{base}}/appointments/{{createAppointment.response.body.data._id}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "cancelled" }

### 11. Deleting a provider with booked appointments is refused -> 400
DELETE {{base}}/providers/{{createProvider.response.body.data._id}}
